[128.844254, "i", "cat > FIXED_SUMMARY.txt << 'EOF'\n=== ALERTMANAGER FIX SUMMARY ===\n\nPROBLEM:\n- Alertmanager was failing to start with YAML parse error at line 51\n- Error: \"found character that cannot start any token\"\n\nROOT CAUSE:\n- Line 51 in alertmanager.yml had incorrect indentation\n- 'send_resolved: false' was indented with 10 spaces instead of 8\n- YAML requires consistent indentation for properties at the same level\n\nFIX APPLIED:\n- Corrected indentation on line 51 from 10 spaces to 8 spaces\n- Matches the indentation pattern of 'channel:' property above it\n- Backup saved as alertmanager.yml.bak\n\nVERIFICATION:\n- Alertmanager is running on port 9093 (PID 670)\n- Health check: OK\n- Cluster status: ready\n- All alert routes intact:\n  * pagerduty-critical (for severity=critical alerts)\n  * slack-warnings (for severity=warning alerts)\n  * team-backend (for service=foo|bar alerts)\n  * default-receiver (catch-all)\n\nINTEGRATIONS PRESERVED:\n- PagerDuty: service_key configured, severity=critical\n- Slack: 4 channels configured (#alerts-"]
[128.844399, "i", "general, #alerts-warnings, #team-backend-alerts, #db-alerts)\n- Templates: slack.tmpl and pagerduty.tmpl loaded successfully\n\nPrometheus rules in /home/user/monitoring/rules/ are compatible with configured routes.\nEOF\n"]
